<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbasid Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/750">750</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abbasid Revolution was the uprising that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid dynasty</a> to power in 750. Launched from Khurasan under the organiser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-muslim">Abu Muslim</a>, it drew on discontent among non-Arab Muslims and supporters of the Prophet's family. It ended Umayyad rule in the east, shifted the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, and is central to the foundation of the Abbasid Caliphate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution.jpg" alt="Abbasid Revolution" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sheperd, William R.; Historical Atlas; New York: Henry Holt and Company, 1911. 53. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caliphate_750.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
